## SQ-CFS-01 | CfB oven gets lit=false on a fresh oven and a full-height shape; oven mixins apply
@group A
@commands boot; `grep -nE "CfbOven(Lit\|LitSync\|Shape\|Renderer)Mixin\|blockheads_additions.mixins\|InvalidInjectionException" logs/latest.log`; `/setblock` a `cookingforblockheads:oven`; probe its block state and shape
@pass `Done (`; no mixin error; the oven's states include `lit`, a fresh oven is `lit=false`; its shape's max y is 1.0 (was 0.9375)
@fails mixin target name (SRG `m_7926_`, `m_49959_`, `m_5940_`, `serverTick` descriptor) wrong for CfB 13.3.4
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
shell grep -nE "CfbOven(Lit|LitSync|Shape|Fuel|Smoking)Mixin|blockheads_additions.mixins|InvalidInjectionException" logs/latest.log | head -12 | cut -c1-260; true
bootreject CfbOven\w*Mixin.*(rror|ailed|could not)
> setblock 300 -60 310 cookingforblockheads:oven[facing=north]
> zc2 state 300 -60 310
waitlog \[zc2\] state 300 -60 310 20
expect \[zc2\] state 300 -60 310: .*lit=false
expect \[zc2\] state 300 -60 310: .*maxY=1\.0
look shell lines: no InvalidInjectionException naming a CfbOven mixin (others in the log are third-party, note them only)

## SQ-CFS-02 | a CfB oven is an FD heat source only while lit; the pot above cooks only then; oven slots kept through the toggles
@group A
@commands tag probe `#farmersdelight:heat_sources`; oven with no fuel, `farmersdelight:cooking_pot` above it with a fast recipe's inputs (`/data merge block`); wait 30 s; then put coal in the oven's fuel slot (`/data get block` first to see the fuel container's NBT key, then `/data merge block`, or a hopper into the fuel side); wait; let the fuel run out
@pass tag lists `cookingforblockheads:oven`; no cooking while unlit; `lit=true` within a tick of burning, the pot finishes the meal; `lit=false` when the fuel runs out and the pot's progress stops; the oven's input, output and tool slots keep their items through each toggle
@fails `CfbOvenLitSyncMixin` not at RETURN of the instance `serverTick`; tag script skipped (`global.CD.on('blockheads_additions')` false)
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
> zq blocktag farmersdelight:heat_sources
> zq rdetail farmersdelight:cooking/tomato_sauce
> setblock 304 -60 310 cookingforblockheads:oven[facing=north]{ItemHandler:{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:potato",Count:3b}]}}
> setblock 304 -59 310 farmersdelight:cooking_pot{Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"farmersdelight:tomato",Count:1b},{Slot:1,id:"farmersdelight:tomato",Count:1b},{Slot:7,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:4b}]}}
> data get block 304 -60 310
sleep 10
> zc2 inv 304 -59 310
> zc2 state 304 -60 310
> data merge block 304 -60 310 {BurnTime:400,CurrentItemBurnTime:400}
sleep 2
> zc2 state 304 -60 310
sleep 12
> zc2 inv 304 -59 310
sleep 10
> zc2 state 304 -60 310
> zc2 inv 304 -59 310
sleep 4
> zc2 inv 304 -59 310
> zc2 inv 304 -60 310
expect blocktag farmersdelight:heat_sources .*cookingforblockheads:oven
expect \[zc2\] state 304 -60 310: .*lit=true
expect \[zc2\] state 304 -60 310: .*lit=false
look (1) the rdetail line gives tomato_sauce's inputs; if they are not 2 tomatoes the pot never starts: BATCH-FAULT, rerun with those inputs. (2) first pot inv (unlit, 10 s): CookTime=0. (3) after BurnTime 400 the oven reads lit=true; 12 s later the pot's CookTime > 0 or the sauce is in slot 6/8. (4) after the burn ran out (about 20 s) lit=false and the two last pot reads 4 s apart show the same CookTime (no progress). (5) last oven inv still holds 0:3 minecraft:potato. data get line: note the fuel slot index (ItemHandler) for the CQ / a rerun with real fuel

## SQ-CFS-03 | skillet cooks only while the oven under it is lit; a Brewin' keg's temperature rises while lit
@group A
@commands same with `farmersdelight:skillet` (block) and a Brewin' keg on a burning oven
@pass skillet cooks only while lit; keg temperature rises while lit
@fails keg tag no longer nests FD heat_sources
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
> setblock 308 -60 310 cookingforblockheads:oven[facing=north]
> setblock 308 -59 310 farmersdelight:skillet[facing=north]
> setblock 312 -60 310 cookingforblockheads:oven[facing=north]
> setblock 312 -59 310 brewinandchewin:keg[facing=north]
> pbot hold c2b minecraft:beef 1
> pbot use c2b 308 -59 310
sleep 6
> zc2 inv 308 -59 310
> zc2 inv 312 -59 310
> data merge block 308 -60 310 {BurnTime:600,CurrentItemBurnTime:600}
> data merge block 312 -60 310 {BurnTime:600,CurrentItemBurnTime:600}
sleep 8
> zc2 inv 308 -59 310
> zc2 inv 312 -59 310
sleep 25
> zc2 inv 308 -59 310
> zc2 state 312 -60 310
> zc2 inv 312 -59 310
look skillet: the beef placed by the bot ("use" line SUCCESS/CONSUME), cooking progress 0 in the unlit read, rising after BurnTime (cooked beef or progress > 0 after 8 s); keg: temperature tag (numeric list) higher while lit than before; after the burn ran out (33 s) the oven lit=false. If the keg has no temperature field in its NBT, mark not judged (client WTHIT)

